12. PAYMENT HOLD AND ESCROW WORKFLOW

The payment-hold system must work with the chat and order system.

Maintain the minimum 24-hour inspection period after confirmed physical receipt.

Use an approved conditional-settlement arrangement with the appropriate payment partner.

Do not pretend that frontend timers or ordinary payment split features are genuine escrow.

Workflow

1. Customer places an order.
2. Customer completes payment.
3. Payment is confirmed.
4. Vendor receives the order.
5. Vendor prepares the product.
6. Vendor dispatches the product or arranges pickup.
7. Delivery or collection is independently confirmed.
8. The inspection countdown starts.
9. Customer inspects the product.
10. Customer accepts the order or opens a dispute.
11. A dispute pauses settlement.
12. If the inspection period expires without a dispute, the order follows the configured release process.
13. Settlement is recorded.

Timer rules

The countdown begins from confirmed physical receipt, not dispatch.

Use server-authoritative timestamps in production.

Do not rely on the customer’s or vendor’s phone clock.

Provide an accurate countdown and deadline in both dashboards and chat.

Allow the administrator to configure a longer inspection period, but never set it below 24 hours.

